{"name":"Café au Lait","hex":"#a57c5b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"café au lait","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Coffee mixed with hot milk as a drink; white coffee;  a serving of this.","Coffee and hot milk served in separate jugs as a breakfast drink;  a serving of this."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a light brown colour like that of coffee with milk.","Of a person: having skin of a light brown colour; also, of a person's skin: having this colour; often  due to mixed black and white parentage or ancestry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caf%C3%A9_au_lait"}],"entries":[{"title":"Café au lait","blocks":[{"text":"Café au lait is coffee with hot milk added. It differs from white coffee, which is coffee with cold milk or other whiteners added."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Caf%C3%A9_au_lait.jpg/330px-Caf%C3%A9_au_lait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caf%C3%A9_au_lait"},{"title":"Coffee (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee is a brownish color that is a representation of a roasted coffee bean. Different types of coffee beans have different colors when roasted—the color coffee represents an average."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee_(color)"},{"title":"Coffeehouse","blocks":[{"text":"A coffeehouse, coffee shop, or café, is an establishment that serves various types of coffee drinks like espresso, latte, americano and cappuccino, as well as other beverages. An espresso bar specializes in serving espresso and espresso-based drinks. Some coffeehouses may serve iced coffee among other cold drinks, as well as non-caffeinated drinks. A coffeehouse may also serve food, such as light snacks, sandwiches, muffins, cakes, breads, pastries or doughnuts. Many doughnut shops in Canada and the U.S. serve coffee to accompany doughnuts, so these can also be classified as coffee shops, although doughnut shops tend to be more casual and serve cheaper fare. In continental Europe, some cafés even serve alcoholic drinks, and in West Asia, coffeehouses may offer a flavored tobacco smoked through a hookah, called shisha in most varieties of Arabic or nargile in Levantine Arabic, Greek, and Turkish."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Caf%C3%A9_de_Flore.jpg/330px-Caf%C3%A9_de_Flore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffeehouse"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Cafe_au_Lait_and_Beignets_New_Orleans.jpg/500px-Cafe_au_Lait_and_Beignets_New_Orleans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Cafe_au_Lait_and_Beignets_New_Orleans.jpg/1280px-Cafe_au_Lait_and_Beignets_New_Orleans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Cafe_au_Lait_and_Beignets_New_Orleans.jpg/500px-Cafe_au_Lait_and_Beignets_New_Orleans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A café au lait and beignets served in Café du Monde, New Orleans","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACafe_au_Lait_and_Beignets_New_Orleans.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Unroasted_coffee.jpg/500px-Unroasted_coffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Unroasted_coffee.jpg/1280px-Unroasted_coffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki